## Recalls Are Happening at a Record Pace

With 509 recalls this year alone and 152 classified as Class I - indicating situations where there is a reasonable probability that the use of the product will cause serious adverse health consequences or death - it's hard to deny that food safety is facing a critical moment. This year's numbers are on track to exceed previous records, with heavy hitters like allergens and Salmonella leading the charge.

## The Worst Offenders

The data from this month highlights recurring issues with several brands. Among them, Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company top the list of the worst offenders, both with a dismal recall grade of F. Moonlight Packing Corporation has had 11 recalls, all Class I. Meanwhile, Ghirardelli Chocolate Company has faced 10 recalls this year, all for products contaminated with Salmonella.

## Recent Recalls You Should Know About

On June 3rd, 2026, several recalls were reported, including products from Legacy Bakehouse LLC, Wawa Beverage Company, and Honeyville, Inc. Legacy Bakehouse's products were affected due to the use of contaminated milk powder from California Dairies leading to Salmonella contamination. Wawa Beverage Company's products were recalled for undeclared milk allergens, and Honeyville, Inc faced issues with Salmonella contamination in its bulk smoothie ingredients.

## A Systemic Issue?

With 83 repeat offenders this year, it begs the question of whether the food industry is adequately addressing its quality control challenges. The recurring nature of these recalls, particularly involving the same brands and similar reasons, suggests systemic weaknesses in supply chain oversight and testing protocols.

## What's Next?

As consumers, we need to stay informed and proactive about food safety announcements, as the consequences of negligence in this area can be dire. Food industry players, on the other hand, should aim for transparency and stringent quality control to rebuild trust.

## Brands to Watch

Today's focus falls squarely on brands like Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company, which have consistently failed to meet safety expectations. If you see recent products from these companies, it might be wise to double-check their recall status before adding them to your shopping cart.
